# Turn the servo torque of one arm on or off.
#
# Both halves travel in one call. Setting an arm through a parameter and then
# triggering the change is two round trips, and a second client arriving in
# between turns the torque off on an arm nobody asked about.

# ARM_LEFT, ARM_RIGHT or ARM_BOTH.
string arm

string ARM_LEFT=left
string ARM_RIGHT=right
string ARM_BOTH=both

# Not called `on`. YAML reads a bare `on` as a boolean, so `ros2 service call`
# hands the field name True instead of a string and refuses the call - which is
# a thing an operator meets while typing at a robot, not while writing code.
bool enable
---
bool success
string message
